numz's modified copies of SeedVR's own (commit e4de8c2: projects/video_diffusion_sr/infer.py and
models/video_vae_v3/modules/attn_video_vae.py). All are under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
That file says what was changed.

It also includes, adapted in seedvr2x/tiling.py (encode_tiled, decode_tiled), the VAE
tiling of ComfyUI-SeedVR2_VideoUpscaler (numz and contributors, commit 4490bd1):
VideoAutoencoderKL's tiled_encode and tiled_decode, in
src/models/video_vae_v3/modules/attn_video_vae.py. They are numz's own, SeedVR's file (commit
e4de8c2: models/video_vae_v3/modules/attn_video_vae.py) leaving both unwritten, under the Apache
License, Version 2.0. That file says what was changed.

It also includes, written in seedvr2x/int8.py from comfy-kitchen's source (Comfy Org,
https://github.com/Comfy-Org/comfy-kitchen, version 0.2.37, commit be003b7), Copyright (c) 2025
Comfy Org, under the Apache License, Version 2.0: its regular Hadamard rotation
(comfy_kitchen/tensor/int8_utils.py) and the arithmetic of its int8 linear's activation
quantizer and dequantization (comfy_kitchen/backends/cuda/ops/int8_linear.cu and
cutlass_gemm_int8.cu), in PyTorch; no comfy-kitchen code runs in seedvr2x. That file says what
it follows and where it differs.

It also includes, written in seedvr2x/kquant.py from llama.cpp's source (ggml-org/llama.cpp,
https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp, tag v0.8.0, commit 8642541), Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The
ggml authors, under the MIT License: the K-quant block formats of Q3_K, Q4_K and Q5_K
(ggml/src/ggml-common.h: block_q3_K, block_q4_K, block_q5_K) and their dequantisation
(ggml/src/ggml-quants.c: dequantize_row_q3_K, dequantize_row_q4_K, dequantize_row_q5_K and
get_scale_min_k4), in PyTorch; no llama.cpp code runs in seedvr2x. That file says what it
follows. llama.cpp's gguf-py package (gguf, MIT) is the reference its tests compare with, and no
dependency of the library.

It also includes TransNetV2's official PyTorch model, seedvr2x/transnetv2/transnetv2_pytorch.py,
copied unchanged from TransNetV2 (https://github.com/soCzech/TransNetV2, commit 85cef72,
inference-pytorch/transnetv2_pytorch.py): TransNetV2, Copyright (c) 2020 Tomáš Souček, under the
MIT License, whose text is beside it, in seedvr2x/transnetv2/LICENSE. seedvr2x pulls its
weights, transnetv2.safetensors, from its own Hugging Face repo (hekmon/seedvr2x), under the same
licence: TransNetV2's official TensorFlow weights converted to PyTorch by its own
inference-pytorch/convert_weights.py, values unchanged, by the repository's
models/transnetv2_weights.py. It also includes code adapted from TransNetV2, under the same
licence: predict_frames' windows (inference/transnetv2.py at that commit), rewritten in
seedvr2x/detector.py to run on frames as they come, after the repository's
research/scripts/scd_scores.py (tnet_predict), whose rewrite tests/test_detector.py copies to hold
them to.
